{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A cut through an ANSI sequence can leave part of a registered credential in stored output, but the required output and cut position are contrived."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A credential matching a phase name can cause a resumed run to skip its remaining stages and report success."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"secret","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Coverage canonicalization can expose a credential embedded in a symlink target filename in the stored result."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A failing gate can expose a multiline environment credential when its separately processed lines are rejoined in a failure excerpt."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Downloading a patch containing literal terminal sequences returns altered source text instead of the stored artifact."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A patch containing literal terminal sequences is changed in the review prompt, potentially obscuring bytes the reviewer should inspect."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"The API-wide transformation can return altered event text and artifact content when those strings contain literal terminal sequences."},{"id":"C2b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A saved test command containing literal terminal sequences is changed on restoration, producing a false blocking audit finding."}]}